<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Golden Gate (Bhaktapur)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1754">1754</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Lu Dhowka</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Golden Gate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhaktapur">Bhaktapur</a> is a gilded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> gateway at the entrance to the royal palace of fifty-five windows in Durbar Square, Bhaktapur, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>. Commissioned by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranajit-malla">Ranajit Malla</a> in 1754, it is decorated with images of the goddess Taleju and Garuda, and is one of the finest examples of Newar metalwork.</p></div>
